# v1.24 FLEET RETRAIN — the price-dispersion cycle, rung 1.
#
# WHY. Both DEFEND-root members hold their objective as one pile and win every
# episode: stacked 0.976 / 0.960 with nearest-teammate distance 0.205 / 0.225
# against a STACK_RADIUS of 1.5 — the whole element in effectively one cell,
# spatially unsound 96-98% of the time. The piling is CHOSEN, not geometric:
# that hypothesis was tested and refuted (2026-08-26). `stacked_rate` became a
# MARKER the same day, so the behaviour now ships and is visible rather than
# blocked; this cycle is the response — make it cost something.
#
# WHAT CHANGED IN cohort/, AND IT IS ONE FIELD. `RewardConfig.bunching_penalty`
# = -0.05: each living agent, each step, pays for every teammate inside
# `bunching_radius` BEYOND THE FIRST. A threshold price at N=1, not a per-step
# one, so a buddy pair pays nothing and the pile pays. N=1 is not a free
# parameter — `stacked_rate` is defined as ">= 2 living teammates within
# STACK_RADIUS", so one free teammate makes the first charged step exactly the
# first stacked step. The priced quantity IS the measured quantity.
#
# THIS IS NOT THE MECHANISM WE STARTED WITH, and the reason is on the record.
# The owner first chose AREA FIRE (casualty coupling) on my recommendation. It
# was armed at burst_fraction=0.5 and REFUTED before job 1: dropping the two
# DEFEND incumbents into the armed world without retraining moved nothing
# (success 1.000->0.980 and 1.000->1.000, nn 0.205->0.207 and 0.225->0.227).
# scripts/burst_engagement_probe.py says why — the two members that pile up are
# the two that are never shot at (0.9 and 0.5 enemy hits/ep against
# platoon_hard's 17.6, cover occupancy under threat 0.996/0.999). A price
# coupled to incoming fire has no channel to charge them. AREA FIRE is reverted
# to OFF and is NOT refuted as a mechanic — it bites hardest where fire is heavy.
#
# THE RUNG IS SIZED FROM MEASUREMENT. Arming a price cannot move a trajectory of
# an already-trained policy, so what each member WOULD pay is arithmetic over
# rollouts that already exist. scripts/bunching_price_calibration.py, N=20, per
# agent per episode at -0.05, against success_team = 60:
#
#   fireteam_defend  -9.75 (16%)    platoon_hard  -4.80 ( 8%)    squad_screen -1.00 (2%)
#   platoon          -9.20 (15%)    squad_recon   -3.50 ( 6%)    patrol_brique -0.70 (1%)
#   defend_brique    -7.90 (13%)    squad         -1.70 ( 3%)    fireteam      -0.55 (1%)
#
# Ladder -0.05 -> -0.10 -> -0.20 declared in docs/prereg-price-dispersion.md.
# This is rung 1. Climbing is a new decision and a new campaign.
#
# THE BAR WAS WRITTEN BEFORE THE MECHANISM WAS PICKED, on purpose.
# docs/prereg-price-dispersion.md, scored by scripts/prereg_dispersion.py against
# incumbents frozen in the matching .json, thresholds pinned by
# tests/test_prereg_dispersion.py. SEPARATES needs, in BOTH DEFEND members:
# stacked < 0.70, nearest-teammate distance up >= 0.50 cells (the DENOMINATOR
# guard — a marker that falls because teammates died is not a win), and success
# non-inferior by one-sided Fisher; plus a Holm-corrected success guard over the
# other seven. platoon and squad_recon are exposed (15% and 6%) and sit in that
# guard: a success loss there reads WALKS, and that is registered, not argued
# after the fact.
#
# WHAT THIS CAMPAIGN FREEZES. `cohort/` at the commit that arms the price.
# A queue launches each job when it reaches it and train.py imports the tree
# that exists at that moment, so no commit may touch `cohort/` until the last
# job lands. Tooling, tests, docs, boards and runs/ stay free to move.
#
# THE SEED BUDGET IS 18 JOBS, NOT 11, and the reason is a finding rather than
# caution: A SEED SEARCH DOES NOT SURVIVE A TREE CHANGE. On the v1.23 transition
# patrol_brique carried 2 of 4 seeds, with one flipping 0.949 -> 0.000. So the
# three scenarios with a bimodal reporting channel — patrol_brique, platoon,
# platoon_hard — each re-run their declared search at 4 seeds. The six
# single-seed scenarios run once. Ordered so the cheap fleet completes first and
# the spares only cost what they are needed for.
#
# AND squad's PROVENANCE EXCEPTION RESOLVES HERE. squad_ctrl_v2_seed12 is the
# one member on a different tree (81a9cec6 vs ee378f01) — my planning error,
# disclosed in the manifest. It gets a job this time.
#
# THE PREFLIGHT WILL REFUSE THESE JOBS AND FORCE=1 IS THE RIGHT ANSWER, for a
# reason that is checkable rather than remembered. Every job re-derives a config
# the record holds. But the v1.23 lesson is that "the tree moved" is NEVER on
# its own a reason to re-run — a tree change at constant OBS_DIM produced
# bit-identical checkpoints five commits apart. OBS_DIM does NOT move here
# (a reward field is not an observation), so that argument is unavailable and
# something stronger is needed: the reward function itself changed, and every
# priced member's per-episode return changes by the measured amounts in the
# table above — 0.55 to 9.75 per agent — which enters the advantage estimate
# from the first update. Trajectories cannot coincide. That is measured, not
# assumed: scripts/bunching_price_calibration.py prints the deltas, and
# tests/test_degraded_regression.py::test_a_reward_price_cannot_move_the_world
# pins the other half — the price moves the reward and NOTHING else, at a
# magnitude 100x the shipped one. So the change is confined to exactly the
# signal the optimizer consumes, and it is non-zero for all nine scenarios.
#
# AND IF THAT ARGUMENT IS WRONG, IT SELF-DISCLOSES. baseline.py's reproduction
# digests report bit-identical pairs, so a member that re-derives its
# predecessor cannot pass silently the way squad_v29_seed14 did (#63). The
# cost of being wrong here is CPU and zero tokens, and it surfaces at seal
# time rather than at publication.
#
# AFTER THIS LANDS: score the bar with
#   scripts/prereg_dispersion.py --manifest --setting bunching_penalty=-0.05
# BEFORE anything is published. Then publish_baseline.py at N=100 (detached),
# baseline.py --seal, results_table.py --write. A MISS supersedes nothing
# without an ask, and WALKS is a miss.
#
# ~18 runs x 25-45 min, sequential in one nohup'd queue.
fireteam_v15               --scenario fireteam        --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12
fireteam_defend_v26        --scenario fireteam_defend --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12
squad_v30                  --scenario squad          --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
squad_recon_v14            --scenario squad_recon     --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
squad_screen_v20           --scenario squad_screen    --total-steps 2500000 --seed 12
defend_brique_v20          --scenario defend_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
platoon_v15_seed12         --scenario platoon         --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
platoon_v16_seed13         --scenario platoon         --total-steps 3000000 --seed 13
platoon_v17_seed14         --scenario platoon         --total-steps 3000000 --seed 14
platoon_v18_seed15         --scenario platoon         --total-steps 3000000 --seed 15
platoon_hard_v8_seed12     --scenario platoon_hard    --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
platoon_hard_v9_seed13     --scenario platoon_hard    --total-steps 3000000 --seed 13
platoon_hard_v10_seed14    --scenario platoon_hard    --total-steps 3000000 --seed 14
platoon_hard_v11_seed15    --scenario platoon_hard    --total-steps 3000000 --seed 15
patrol_brique_v46_seed12   --scenario patrol_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
patrol_brique_v47_seed18   --scenario patrol_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 18
patrol_brique_v48_seed19   --scenario patrol_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 19
patrol_brique_v49_seed14   --scenario patrol_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 14

# --- APPENDED 2026-08-31 (autocycle), while the queue was still reading this file ---
# squad_v30 (the campaign's ONLY squad job) COLLAPSED: succ 74% -> 0%, ep return
# 49.4 -> 1.4, ep length 217 -> 450 (clock out 1.000), bunching 0.291 -> 0.013.
# The marker "improved" because the mission vanished. platoon seed 12 collapsed
# the same way; platoon seed 13 is at 96%, so the failure is seed-CONTINGENT and
# spares are the declared response (the v1.23 finding: a seed search does not
# survive a tree change, and a reward change is a tree change).
# squad was budgeted ONE job because it was not thought bimodal. It is now.
# Three spares so the campaign can land with a squad member instead of a hole.
# Appended, never rewritten: the queue holds an open fd on this file and a
# rewrite would point it at a deleted inode.
squad_v31_seed13           --scenario squad           --total-steps 3000000 --seed 13
squad_v32_seed14           --scenario squad           --total-steps 3000000 --seed 14
squad_v33_seed15           --scenario squad           --total-steps 3000000 --seed 15
